The House of the Dragon season finale  was pretty brutal but it could have been  terrifying the first season of The Game  of Thrones prequel includes several  intense birth scenes that emphasize the  brutal nature of childbirth in Westeros  indeed the very first episode features a  particularly violent and bloody scene in  which Queen Emma's labor goes horribly  wrong and neither the mother nor the  baby survives episode 6 features two  more birth scenes modern Witch Princess  rhaenyra Targaryen delivers her baby and  then immediately marches through the red  keep trailing blood and another in which  Elena valarian commits suicide by Dragon  after her own labor goes awry I reached  the limit of my art yet the series saves  us most disturbing birth scene for the  season 1 finale in which we see rhaenyra  enter labor prematurely and deliver a  deformed stillborn baby named vicenia  although the camera doesn't linger too  long on baby visenya within the episode  a recent Instagram post from the series  prosthetic makeup designer Barry Gower  gives us a closer look at the baby's  Design Within the episode itself it's  hard to get a good look at the stillborn  for senya as she is covered in blood and  held tightly in the arms of rhaenyra but  gower's post illuminates some of the  finer details with two brightly lit  images of baby vicenia against the black  background the first one highlights her  to formed nose and sunken face and the  second shows her cone-shaped skull the  most striking deformity present in these  two images is the numerous dragon-like  scales that cover vessenia's head chest  and back the second image shows that she  has an abundance of these scales on the  back of her head and running down her  spine and that the back of her head  features an almost horn-like protrusion  that accounts for a skull's shape  considering the immense amount of  details shown in this small model is  surprising that these scales are so  obscured in the episode itself  especially since they are specifically  mentioned in the series Source material  Fire and Blood In The Fire and Blood  chapter the dying of the Dragons a fool  known as mushroom claims that rhaenyra  curse baby senya during her premature  birth calling her a monster and yelling  for her to get out mushroom goes on to  allege that these curses bore fruit when  the vicenia was finally born saying when  the baby at last came forth she proved  indeed a monster a stillborn girl  twisted and malformed with a hole in her  chest where her heart should have been  and a stubby scaled tail it's worth  mentioning that mushrooms account of the  events in Fire and Blood is considered  to be a reliable and exaggerated so it  makes sense that the design team chose  to tone down his version of vicenya for  House of the Dragon while still making  her somewhat dragon-like although this  silicon model does not appear to include  the tale it's clear that the Prosthetics  team paid close attention to the details  of the senya's malformed appearance and  scales culminating in the design we see  in gower's Instagram post it's hard to  grasp the immense attention to detail  that went into this model when watching  the episode itself due to visenya's  incredibly brief appearance though  gower's post makes it abundantly clear  that the Aesthetics Department went  above and beyond to make this final  birth scene really stand out amongst all  the others in the series
 

